  workspace?: string | null,
}): Promise<unknown>"},{"path":"tools["ai-memory"].memory_message_send","description":"Send a message to an ai-memory project inbox. Same-project delivery is allowed. Use this when the user asks to "send a report", "notify", or "leave a message for" the agent working in a different project/repo, or wants an agent there to do something and you should NOT pull that project's context into this session. This is the ONLY tool that lands anything in a project's inbox: a wiki page written into the target project with memory_write_page is NOT a message and is never surfaced as one. Compose a SELF-CONTAINED request in `body` (the recipient works from it alone) and address it with the REQUIRED `to_workspace` + `to_project`. Optional `to_agent` restricts claiming to that registered harness; the recipient project must have a session for it. Omit it for shared project mail. The recipient project must already exist ÔÇö an unknown target is rejected, not created. The message waits in the recipient's inbox until a session there pops it exactly once (memory_message_pop) or you retract it (memory_message_cancel). Set optional `nature` to `measured`, `reported`, `inferred`, or `unknown` (the default); `measured` requires non-empty bounded `evidence`. Sender is the current project only for session-aware clients; static MCP clients MUST set `from_workspace`+`from_project` (a guessed sender is refused). `from_agent` is for static clients whose session does not record the sender harness. Body is secret-scrubbed and size-capped. Returns `{ "message_id": ... }`.","signature":"tools["ai-memory"].memory_message_send({
  /**
   * Recipient workspace. REQUIRED ÔÇö names the other project's inbox to
   * deliver into. Must already exist (an agent must have run there at least
   * once); an unknown recipient is rejected rather than creating a dead
   * inbox nobody reads.
   */
  to_workspace: string,
  /** Recipient project, together with `to_workspace`. REQUIRED. */
  to_project: string,
  /**
   * Optional harness that alone may claim the message (`codex`, `grok`,
   * `claude-code`, ...). Other harnesses in the recipient project cannot
   * pop it, even by id. Omit for shared project mail. The harness must
   * have at least one registered session in the recipient project.
   * @default null
   */
  to_agent?: string | null,
  /**
   * The message body: the request for the recipient agent. Compose a
   * self-contained prompt ÔÇö the recipient works from this alone, without
   * your project's context.
   */
  body: string,
  /** Optional one-line subject shown in the recipient's inbox listing. @default null */
