  from_agent?: string | null,
  /**
   * Sender project override. Session-aware clients may omit it to send from
   * the current project. Static MCP clients pass it with `from_workspace` to
   * name the sending project explicitly.
   * @default null
   */
  from_project?: string | null,
  /** Sender workspace override, together with `from_project`. @default null */
  from_workspace?: string | null,
}): Promise<unknown>"},{"path":"tools["reason-network"].ask_user","description":"Ask your own user, with a pop-up on their screen, and wait for their answer: approve or deny, maybe with a note. For when a teammate's agent asks you for something only your user can OK and they may not be watching. The answer is theirs, given in the pop-up.","signature":"tools["reason-network"].ask_user({
  /** Antigravity: the conversation id supplied by your Reason Network hook. Other agents omit it. @default null */
  session_id?: string | null,
  /** What they need to decide: who asks for what, and why. */
  question: string,
  /**
   * When it's about a teammate's message, its id (the `id="ÔÇª"` of their `<reason-message>`): your user sees that
   * request in the pop-up, and its sender gets the answer signed by this machine.
   * @default null
   */
  about?: string | null,
}): Promise<unknown>"},{"path":"tools["ai-memory"].memory_handoff_accept","description":"Fetch an OPEN cross-agent handoff and mark it accepted. IMPORTANT: handoffs are SINGLE-USE. The SessionStart hook automatically consumes the handoff at session-start and prepends the content to your context ÔÇö when you see a block starting with '­ƒôÑ ai-memory: pending handoff from previous session' anywhere in your context, that IS the handoff. `status`: `claimed` (THIS call won it; see `handoff`), `consumed_by_hook` (your SessionStart took it; answer from that block), `none_pending` (nothing to claim, or a hook took it for a client that does not forward its session id: do NOT answer 'no handoff exists' before checking your context). Call this tool only when you BOTH don't see a prepended block AND the user explicitly asks for a handoff (e.g. a hook script ran with no stdout capture). Prefer memory_handoff_list first in that case, then pass the listed `handoff_id` here to claim that exact row. Omitting `handoff_id` claims the latest eligible open handoff.","signature":"tools["ai-memory"].memory_handoff_accept({
  /**
   * Set the receiving cwd so automatic handoffs from that directory or a
   * path-boundary ancestor are eligible.
   * **Omit unless the user explicitly asks about a handoff from a
